@startuml activity-fr-17
' Report §2.1 — FR-17 Build a personal agenda from natural language (Agent 1).
' Source: ConciergeController, AgendaRequest, AgendaApplicationService.buildAgenda/verify,
' AgendaToolsFactory, AgendaTools, LangChain4jAgendaAgentFactory, AgendaBuilder,
' RestCatalogClient, RestRegistrationClient, ClashDetector, GlobalExceptionHandler.
!include include/style.iuml
!include include/activity.iuml

title FR-17 — Build a personal agenda from natural language

|Attendee|
start
:POST /api/v1/concierge/agenda
{attendeeId, interests (free text)};

|concierge-service|
if (attendeeId or interests blank,
or interests over 2000 characters?) then (yes)
  $ERR:400 VALIDATION_FAILED;
  stop
else (no)
endif
:BuildAgendaCommand;
:AgendaToolsFactory.create()
a fresh AgendaTools with an empty dossier;
:LangChain4jAgendaAgentFactory.agentFor(tools);
if (GEMINI_API_KEY set and a
ChatModel available?) then (no)
  $ERR:502 LLM_UNAVAILABLE;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
:AgendaBuilder.buildAgenda(attendeeId, interests)
system prompt + the attendee's own words;

repeat
  |Gemini|
  :model turn: request tool calls,
  or give the final answer;
  |concierge-service|
  if (tool calls requested?) then (yes)
    repeat
      switch (tool requested)
      case (searchSessions)
        :searchSessions(track, day, speaker, keyword)
        via CatalogPort → RestCatalogClient;
        |event-catalog-service|
        :GET /api/v1/sessions/search
        ?track&day&speaker&q;
        |concierge-service|
        :add the sessions to the dossier
        (REST failure → empty list);
      case (getSessionAvailability)
        :getSessionAvailability(sessionId)
        via RegistrationPort → RestRegistrationClient;
        |registration-service|
        :GET /api/v1/sessions/{id}/availability;
        |concierge-service|
        :seats remaining / full
        (404 or failure → "unknown");
      case (getAttendeeRegistrations)
        :getAttendeeRegistrations(attendeeId)
        via RegistrationPort → RestRegistrationClient;
        |registration-service|
        :GET /api/v1/attendees/{id}/registrations;
        |concierge-service|
        :sessions already booked
        (failure → empty list);
      case (detectTimeClashes)
        :detectTimeClashes(sessionIds)
        ClashDetector.detect over the dossier
        — local, deterministic Java;
      endswitch
    repeat while (more tool calls this turn?) is (yes) not (no)
    :return the tool results to the model;
  else (no)
  endif
repeat while (tools were called, and fewer than 12 round trips?) is (yes) not (final answer)

|Gemini|
:structured output: ProposedAgenda
{items [sessionId, rationale], summary};

|concierge-service|
:AgendaApplicationService.verify(proposed, dossier)
— the model's answer is checked in code;
repeat
  :next proposed item, in the model's order;
  if (8 sessions (maxAgendaItems) already accepted?) then (yes)
    :drop it and count it;
  elseif (session not in the dossier
  (never retrieved, or invented)?) then (yes)
    :drop it, add a note;
  elseif (already on the agenda?) then (yes)
    :drop it, add a note;
  elseif (ClashDetector.firstConflict with an
  accepted session?) then (yes)
    :drop it, add a note naming the overlap;
  else (no)
    :accept it with the model's rationale;
  endif
repeat while (more proposed items?) is (yes) not (no)
$OK:200 OK AgendaResponse
{attendeeId, summary, items, notes};

|Attendee|
:reads a clash-free agenda,
with a note for every dropped session;
stop

note right
  <b>Model failures</b> (GlobalExceptionHandler):
  RateLimitException → 429 LLM_RATE_LIMITED
  TimeoutException → 504 LLM_TIMEOUT
  other LangChain4jException → 502 LLM_UNAVAILABLE
  More than 12 tool round trips → LangChain4j throws
  a plain RuntimeException, which no handler maps
  (Spring's default 500).
  Full sessions are kept off the agenda by the prompt
  only: verify() does not re-check availability.
end note
@enduml
